  "notes": "Modified cash basis audit. Governmental receipts/disbursements from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances Total column (pp8-11); the statement rolls forward fund balance (385,377 -> 358,019), which includes Due from Proprietary Funds 25,733, so fund balance is filled and beginning/ending cash left null (governmental cash 322,303 + County Treasurer 9,983 at year end, p7; no beginning cash printed). Transfers in/out from the Total column (after the Adjustments column eliminations, p11). Business-type from the proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Fund Net Position Totals column (pp16-17), measure net position; no single total revenue line is printed, so business receipts total = operating + nonoperating revenues; disbursements total 1,067,156 printed on the Statement of Activities (p3) = operating 966,104 + bond issue costs 31,865 + interest 69,187. Loan proceeds 1,480,000 appear only in the cash flow statement (p18). Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position (pp1-2) since it includes capital assets and debt; the Adjustments column is tagged fund_type eliminations. Detail: budget comparison schedule (total primary government, pp20-21) revenue lines and business-type disbursement lines (Electric, Trash, Sewer, Water; no detail total since the governmental lines are left out); governmental disbursement detail taken from the more detailed Schedule of Expenditures by fund and object (p22) instead of the budget schedule's governmental function lines (General Government 188,311, Public Safety 29,009, Public Works 188,538, Culture and Recreation 104,243, which also include transfers), to avoid double counting. Budget revenue 'Local Receipts: Other' 2,674,318 is mixed governmental and business-type. Electrical statistical data (p23) is not a money schedule. Read pages 1-23 of 23"
}
